      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/9fc29f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-09-06T17:40:36.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>One of my few problems with the SCRPG is Lieutenants and how sometimes they can be even worse than Villains. &nbsp;A villain you can nickel and dime down, where as Lieutenants can take up to a minimum of six hits to go down. &nbsp;And, a lieutenant can (technically) take more damage than a villain.</p>\n<p>A Villain that gets hit by an orbital death Laser can get taken out in one shot, but a D6 Lieutenant? &nbsp;He could (rules as written) take 9999 Damage and he’d still only degrade 1 step. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Rediculus you say? &nbsp;Sure. But I had Wraith do around 20ish Damage in the starter kit, enough to do serious damage to a villain, but it only degrades a Lieutenant from a d10 to d8?</p>\n<p>My optional rule is that if a Lieutenant suffers damage from a single attack that deals damage equal to twice their die size, they get automatically taken out (as if a minion failed a save. &nbsp;So 8 damage to a d4 minion, 12 Damage to a d6, 16 Damage to a d8 and so on.</p>\n<p>Thoughts?</p>",
